WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.800
Public model releases form an ecosystem of candidate reference models.

2
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:14.600
Fine-tuning, pruning, merging, distillation, and quantization can alter a model. Combined, these operations may
obscure its origin.

3
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:20.600
A suspect model appears. Which reference model might it come from?

4
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:28.600
AttnDiff uses matched prompts. A small word change creates a semantic conflict, revealing how attention
responds.

5
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:37.600
For every layer and head, attention maps are aligned when needed. Original attention is subtracted from
corrupted attention.

6
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:46.600
Singular value decomposition extracts compact spectral descriptors. Across layers, heads, and probes, these
form a model fingerprint.

7
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:54.600
The same probes independently fingerprint each model. Centered kernel alignment compares their structure,
even when feature dimensions differ.

8
00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.000
Fingerprint similarity provides evidence for tracing model lineage.
